  body: "# Claimant Commitment as the legacy jobseeker’s agreement\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nFor
    the legacy JSA regime described in the source, the Claimant Commitment name introduced from 2013 refers
    legally to a jobseeker’s agreement; the agreement is subject to conditions and referral to a decision
    maker.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 21810 excludes IS from the agreement requirement. DMG 21811
    expressly directs UC and New Style JSA to ADM. A shared label does not establish the same legal instrument
    or rule across benefits. The claimant-requested referral, reasonableness and full agreement conditions
    remain important.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 21810, PDF page 199](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=199)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 21: Jobseeker’s Allowance Labour market questions, special conditions for JSA(Cont)
    and jobseeking periods.\n- [DMG 21811, PDF page 199](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=199)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 21: Jobseeker’s Allowance Labour market questions, special conditions for JSA(Cont)
    and jobseeking periods.\n- [DMG 21840, PDF page 205](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=205)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 21: Jobseeker’s Allowance Labour market questions, special conditions for JSA(Cont)
    and jobseeking periods.\n- [DMG 21841, PDF page 205](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a8eee245a0c25165ae4658d/dmg-v-4-ch-21.pdf#page=205)
    — DMG Vol 4 Ch 21: Jobseeker’s Allowance Labour market questions, special conditions for JSA(Cont)
    and jobseeking periods.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation of selected
    passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required. Source acquisition,
    source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\nThis is an
    independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice, an entitlement
    decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes and characters.
    No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is claimed by this
    record.\n\n- `dmg-vol4-ch21`: PDF SHA-256 `d9fc5e120f85cb69386c9009d97ed2b33844523429224eded21be3c5003693e2`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `82d02218371af05595ac356e9c2f48f5434eb15adf97f0d0d057294c33b099c1`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-availability
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The decision-maker referral concerns whether the agreement would enable the claimant
      to satisfy availability as well as the other stated tests.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch21/0205
      quote: "21840 Emp Os may refer a proposed JSAg to a DM to determine whether1\n\n\n1. if claimants
        were to do what is in the proposed JSAg, they would satisfy\n\n\n      1.1 the availability condition
        or\n\n\n      1.2 the ASE condition and\n\n\n2. it is reasonable to expect the claimant to have
        to do what is in the proposed JSAg (see DMG 21850 -\n21851).\n\n\n                           \
        \                                                           1 JS Act 95, s 9(6)"
      locator: DMG 21840
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-actively-seeking
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The same referral also addresses actively seeking employment and reasonableness; a
      signed document alone does not resolve weekly activity.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch21/0205
      quote: "21840 Emp Os may refer a proposed JSAg to a DM to determine whether1\n\n\n1. if claimants
        were to do what is in the proposed JSAg, they would satisfy\n\n\n      1.1 the availability condition
        or\n\n\n      1.2 the ASE condition and\n\n\n2. it is reasonable to expect the claimant to have
        to do what is in the proposed JSAg (see DMG 21850 -\n21851).\n\n\n                           \
        \                                                           1 JS Act 95, s 9(6)"
      locator: DMG 21840
    - page: page/dmg-vol4-ch21/0156
      quote: "21573 Details of what the claimant has agreed to do to satisfy the ASE test will be in the
        claimant's JSAg.\nBut claimants must in each week take the steps that give them their best chance
        of getting employment\nand this might not always be the same as the steps agreed in the JSAg."
      locator: DMG 21573
